        "Yellow"
      ],
      "cost": "1",
      "specified": null,
      "z": null,
      "power": null,
      "name": "Turles's Power Ball",
      "characters": [],
      "traits": [],
      "skill": "[field]<br>[auto] If your Leader Card is a green or yellow \u226aSaiyan\u226b card: At the end of a turn in which this card was placed in a Battle Area, you may choose 1 \u226aGreat Ape\u226b card with an energy cost of 4 in your hand and play it in your opponent's Battle Area with its skills negated for the game. If you do, draw 2 cards.<br>[activate: main][once per turn]{1}: Choose up to 1 of your opponent's \u226aGreat Ape\u226b cards with an energy cost of 4 or less and gain control of it until the end of the turn.<br>[activate: battle] Place this card in its owner's Drop Area: Choose up to 1 of your cards with <Turles> in its character name and it gets +6000 power for the battle.",
      "backName": null,
      "backSkill": null
    },
    "faq": [
      {
        "name": "Turles's Power Ball",
        "qa": [
          {
            "q": "You use this card\u2019s [Auto] skill to play {P-042 Great Ape Prince Vegeta} in your opponent\u2019s Battle Area, which your opponent then uses in a combo. Does {P-042 Great Ape Prince Vegeta}\u2019s [Auto] skill activate?",
            "a": "No, it doesn\u2019t."
          },
          {
            "q": "You use this card\u2019s [Auto] skill to play {P-042 Great Ape Prince Vegeta} in your opponent\u2019s Battle Area, which your opponent then uses in a combo. At the end of the battle, whose Drop Area is {P-042 Great Ape Prince Vegeta} placed in?",
            "a": "You own the card, so it\u2019s placed in your Drop Area."
          },
          {
            "q": "You use this card\u2019s [Auto] skill to play a\u300aGreat Ape\u300b card in your opponent\u2019s Battle Area with its skills negated, which you gain control of with this card\u2019s [Activate : Main] skill during your next turn. Can you activate the \u300aGreat Ape\u300b card\u2019s skills?",
            "a": "No. The \u300aGreat Ape\u300b card\u2019s skills remain negated."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
